description:
Connect the UI to the new backend graph traversal endpoint.

## Background
Backend v0.2.18 added `GET /nodes/api/nodes/{type}/{label}/graph?depth=N` which returns a node with all connected nodes and links.

## Requirements
- Add `getNodeGraph(nodeType, label, depth)` method to graph-service.js
- Handle success/error responses
- Cache results to avoid redundant fetches

## API Response Format
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "root": "Feature-11",
  "depth": 1,
  "nodes": [{"label", "title", "node_type", "status"}],
  "links": [{"source", "target", "link_type"}]
}
```

## Implementation
```javascript
async getNodeGraph(nodeType, label, depth = 1) {
    const response = await fetch(
        `${this.baseUrl}/nodes/api/nodes/${nodeType}/${label}/graph?depth=${depth}`
    );
    return response.json();
}
```
